{
    "test_name": "MOB.580_AssetVerify_Sort_Ordering",
    "details": {
        "name": "MOB.580_AssetVerify_Sort_Ordering",
        "type": "browser",
        "status": "paused",
        "message": "`MOB.580` **Sorting actually reorders the list** \u2014 the SB block's last open item.\n- READ-ONLY. Changes only the sort selection.\n- **Nothing in this suite proved this before.** MOB.340/530 prove the sort modal opens;\n  MOB.810 proves a choice persists to `sessionStorage`. Neither shows the rows came out\n  in that order.\n- \u2b50 The proof reads the rendered NAMES and checks them against the app's own comparator\n  (`localeCompare`) \u2014 ASC is the sorted order, DESC is its exact reverse. It does **not**\n  hardcode which asset comes first: `\u26a1 Tank 0000` collates before `A/C Motor 0002`, and\n  the old hardcoded pair read a correct app as broken for two runs.\n- Both `A/C Motor 0002` and `Tank 0000` must be found before anything is compared, so it\n  cannot pass on an empty or half-rendered list (trap 5).\n- Leaves the Asset sort set in `sessionStorage`. Harmless: every test that clicks an\n  asset now targets it **by name**, not by position.\n- The three proofs are `soft`: a red one still fails THIS test, but it no longer aborts\n  the run \u2014 on 2026-09-09 the ascending proof took its suite's other 7 children down with\n  it, and none of them had run.\n- Each proof is preceded by an `optional` **DIAG** reading `mobile-Asset-sort`, which\n  separates *the app never took the selection* from *the app took it and did not\n  reorder*.",
        "tags": [
            "Mobile",
            "env:dev",
            "Asset Verification",
            "read-only",
            "SB",
            "module:asset-verify"
        ],
        "locations": [
            "gcp:us-west2"
        ],
        "config": {
            "assertions": [],
            "config_variables": [
                {
